cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its certificates, please cite the paper and this archive."
title: "Verifier for \"A proof of Borcea's quadratic variance conjecture\""
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bouthat
    given-names: Ludovick
    affiliation: "University of Delaware"
  - family-names: Fallat
    given-names: Shaun
    affiliation: "University of Regina"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Borcea's conjecture
  - Sendov's conjecture
  - critical points of polynomials
  - interval arithmetic
  - computer-assisted proof
abstract: >-
  Exact replay of the computer-assisted part of the proof of Borcea's quadratic
  variance conjecture: two certificates cover every degree 4 <= n <= 2047
  (150,845 three-parameter regions for degrees 4-26 and 27,429 two-parameter
  regions for degrees 27-2047), and the verifier re-checks every region with
  directed integer interval arithmetic. Python 3.10+, standard library only.
